    "bio": "a Representative from Indiana; born in Gary, Lake County, Ind., August 13, 1949; graduated from Andrean High School, Merrillville, Ind., 1967; B.S., Indiana University Northwest, Gary, Ind., 1970; J.D., University of Notre Dame School of Law, Notre Dame, Ind., 1973; LL.M., Georgetown University Law Center, Washington, D.C., 1982; lawyer, private practice; staff, United States House of Representatives Committee on Appropriations, 1977-1980; staff, United States House of Representatives Committee on the Budget, 1980-1982; elected as a Democrat to the Ninety-ninth and to the seventeen succeeding Congresses (January 3, 1985-January 3, 2021); was not a candidate for reelection to the One Hundred Seventeenth Congress in 2020.",
